// Test: bugfixes/com001_capability_class_method_this_receiver
// Grammar: capability_decl · class_decl.can_clause · method_call on capability-typed param
// Semantic: COM001 (fingerprints 93df7710de8f / 40d63810 / f9b020dc / 8d4f74b1
//   / 58bb119efe2e, all 2026-07-19). CallCapability dispatch through a
//   bridge function that takes a capability-typed parameter.
//
// Root cause: type_inference.rs::infer_method marked any method on a class
//   with no parent and no fields as `is_static=true`. That was correct for
//   pure utility classes (avoided the body_uses_this() false-positive from
//   fp df5b8c9b1021) but wrong for classes that declare `can C` — their
//   methods MUST accept `this` because CallCapability dispatch pushes the
//   receiver as the first argument. Marking Session.save static dropped
//   `this` from the WASM signature; the dispatcher then left `this`
//   unconsumed on the stack, breaking the `if (Result T)` block's stack
//   invariant and tripping wasmparser with "values remaining on stack at
//   end of block".
//
// Fix (0.33.109+): src/typechecker/type_inference.rs adds
//   `has_capabilities` to the non-static condition:
//     is_static = !(has_parent || has_fields || has_capabilities)
//   A class that declares `can C` has instance methods regardless of its
//   field/parent state.
//
// This pin covers the non-void return case: `boolean save()` on a class
//   that declares `can Persist`, invoked via `Registry.save(target)` where
//   `target: Persist`. The whole chain — Registry.save is a static method,
//   its body does `return target.save()` which is a CallCapability with
//   `Result(I32)` block type, one arm (Session), Session.save now correctly
//   has `this` as its first param.
//
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.109
//
// Expected output:
//   true

start:
	Session s = Session()
	boolean ok = Registry.save(s)
	print(ok.toString())

can Persist:
	boolean save()

class Registry
	functions:
		boolean save(Persist target)
			return target.save()

class Session can Persist
	functions:
		public:
			boolean save()
				return true
